  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 8.3. Increased capacity of member States to integrate social protection in comprehensive policy responses to support and protect workers and employers during their life and work transitions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">FORTHCOMING: In the context of the COVID-19 pandemic crisis, an Emergency Unemployment and Employment Stabilization Fund (EUESF) was designed by the Jordanian Social Security Corporation (SSC) with the support of the ILO, to provide short-term income support and extend social security coverage to informal workers, including refugees and migrant workers. The fund is expected to be established in the course of the last quarter of 2021. Following a participatory approach, the technical and operation design was refined and approved involving all tripartite constituents. A Technical Steering Committee for the Extension of Coverage was established in April 2021 and is responsible for the implementation of EUESF.
Two social dialogue sessions were held (one in September 2020 and another one in June 2021), with the participation of a total of eight different social partners (government, workers and employers&apos; representatives) and civil society organizations to refine the technical and operational design of Phase I of EUESF and provide inputs on areas of collaboration and focus for a prospective Phase II. The ILO led the process of the design refinement, in consultation with all tripartite constituents and aligned with the national regulatory framework, including the latest bylaws that regulate the inclusion of the self-employed under the SSC, and the agricultural workers bylaws that define the framing of these workers under the labour law. All preparatory work has been completed and the Implementation Agreement is ready to be signed by the ILO and SSC, which is expected to happen by end of the third quarter of 2021. The ILO is an active member of the Technical Steering Committee; this committee has met at least once a month since its formation in April 2021.

In February 2021, the ILO published the study &quot;Opportunities for extending social security coverage in Jordan&quot; whose recommendations were key to inform the refinement of the Emergency Unemployment and Employment Stabilization Fund (EUESF) design.
The ILO supported SSC in the organization of the social dialogue, including engagement of different participants, delivery of preparatory briefings, and follow up on matters discussed and actions agreed. These social dialogue initiatives have given the opportunity for all partners to endorse the technical design of the EUESF while engaging on a broader discussion regarding the extension of social security coverage to informal workers, including refugees and migrant workers.</narrative>
   </description>
